; an occurrence marker on an inline (parenthesized) ARRAY group — `[* (int, tstr)]` — used to be
; silently dropped, narrowing the group to exactly-once: the generated decoder then rejected
; spec-valid CBOR carrying any other repetition count (a round-trip test can't see this; only data
; from another conformant producer does). Rejected gracefully instead — the marker on the inline
; group is honored, not narrowed away. The fix's message recommends naming the group
; (`pair = (int, tstr)`, `a = [* pair]`) or dropping the parentheses for a single-element group
; (`[* int]`). Flipping this row to `ok` requires REAL `Vec<Synthesized>` support (a candidate
; feature), not a decay back to silent narrowing. `[1*1 (…)]` stays `ok`: exactly-once IS the
; semantics, so flattening the group away is sound there.
a = [* (int, tstr)]
